WEBVTT

01-01
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.823
Welcome to Week Three.

01-02
00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:06.696
This lesson begins with a question raised by our work in Lab Eight.

01-03
00:00:06.876 --> 00:00:13.916
If a model fits the observations closely, how much confidence should
we place in those observations?

01-04
00:00:14.096 --> 00:00:24.229
We will examine thermodynamic consistency first, then move to a
different question: when does a liquid mixture separate into two
stable liquids?

01-05
00:00:24.409 --> 00:00:28.676
The lesson replaces our classroom session during the holiday.

01-06
00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:38.627
Allow about three hours altogether, including watching, calculations,
Lab investigations, a break, and the closing reflection.

01-07
00:00:38.807 --> 00:00:41.879
The recording is only one part of that time.

01-08
00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:46.773
Keep your own answers and pause whenever an activity is assigned.

02-01
00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:54.573
Start by opening the four-page practice worksheet and the three-page
Lab guide.

02-02
